From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:52:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Print layer trace only with VIDEOSTREAMSWSI_DEBUG

The layer printed a line on stdout for vkCreateInstance,
vkDestroyInstance, vkCreateDevice (plus the instance pointer),
vkDestroyDevice and both extension enumerations. That is useful while
debugging the layer and noise everywhere else: every Vulkan or Zink
application printed it, several times per start, and it filled OBS's
logs.

The lines are now printed only when the VIDEOSTREAMSWSI_DEBUG
environment variable is set. Messages for unimplemented entry points in
Wsi.cpp still go to stderr unconditionally, since they report a real
limitation.
---
 Layer.cpp | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Layer.cpp b/Layer.cpp
index 656cea1..59ca0a8 100644
--- a/Layer.cpp
+++ b/Layer.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <pthread.h>
 
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
 #include <map>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -155,11 +157,24 @@ LayerDevice *LayerDevice::FromHandle(VkDevice device)
 }
 
 
+// Trace output for each layer entry point. It was printed unconditionally
+// and ended up in every application's log (OBS printed it on every context
+// creation). Set VIDEOSTREAMSWSI_DEBUG to see it.
+static bool
+TraceEnabled()
+{
+	static const bool enabled = getenv("VIDEOSTREAMSWSI_DEBUG") != NULL;
+	return enabled;
+}
+
+#define TRACE(...) do { if (TraceEnabled()) printf(__VA_ARGS__); } while (0)
+
+
